# Change the prototype

Work from what the designer asks for, and from the notes they left on the preview.

## Where the changes come from

1. First try to read the pending notes from Agentation through its MCP connection.
2. If there is no connection, say so plainly and ask the designer to use Agentation's copy button on
   the preview and paste the copied notes here. Never invent notes.
3. A note can also be a plain request typed in the chat.

## Apply each note

1. Match the note to the screen, state and element it points at.
2. For a change to one component on one screen, change it where the prototype uses it. Do not
   restyle or change the product component for everyone.
3. For a color, spacing or text style, use an existing token. Use the closest existing token only
   when it is clearly the same intent; otherwise ask the designer before inventing anything new.
4. If a note asks for a brand decision, a change in how the product really behaves, or a component
   the product does not have, do not do it here. Say so and offer to describe it as a proposal for
   engineers.
5. Do only what the note asks.

## Verify, then resolve

1. Check the result in the preview: every affected screen and state, in each theme and screen size
   the prototype supports.
2. Resolve a note only after that check passes, and only through Agentation's own resolve action.
   Until then it stays pending. Never resolve a note you did not verify.
3. Tell the designer which screens and states changed and which notes are resolved or still open.

Next step: run `design-space-preview` to look again, or `design-space-ready` when the prototype is
finished.
